[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Flaky Tests Management and Root Cause Analysis"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Flaky tests are automated tests that can pass and fail under the same code conditions, undermining trust in CI/CD pipelines. This tutorial covers strategies for identifying, managing, and performing root cause analysis (RCA) on flaky tests in automation testing frameworks."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Common Causes of Test Flakiness"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Asynchronous Operations: Relying on arbitrary timeouts (Thread.sleep) instead of explicit waits."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Test Interdependence: Tests sharing state or executing in a strict, fragile sequence."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Environment Issues: Network latency, resource constraints, or database locks."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"UI Rendering Delays: Animations or lazy-loaded components triggering element interception errors."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Implementing Retries and Quarantine"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"While fixing the root cause is the ultimate goal, managing flaky tests in the interim prevents pipeline blockages. Many frameworks like TestNG or Jest support built-in retry mechanisms."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"@Test(retryAnalyzer = RetryAnalyzer.class)
public void potentiallyFlakyTest() {
    driver.get("https://example.com/dashboard");
    Assert.assertTrue(driver.findElement(By.id("analytics-widget")).isDisplayed());
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Root Cause Analysis (RCA) Workflow"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Step 1: Isolate the failure by running the test repeatedly in headless and headed modes."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Step 2: Inspect execution artifacts, including screenshots, video recordings, and network HAR files."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Step 3: Replace implicit or static waits with robust conditional polling mechanisms."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"// Good Practice: Explicit Wait instead of Thread.sleep
WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
WebElement element = wait.until(ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(By.id("submit-btn")));
element.click();"},{"order":16,"type":"subheading","text":"4. Best Practices for Prevention"},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Ensure test isolation by resetting application state before and after each execution."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Mock external third-party services and APIs to ensure deterministic responses."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Track flakiness metrics over time to identify brittle modules or components in the system."}]
